#. module: approval
#: model:ir.model.fields,help:approval.field_ir_attachment__approval_requirement_id
msgid ""
"Which of the category's required documents this file IS. The requester says "
"so; nothing infers it. Before this column the confirm-time check ran a "
"bipartite matching over file NAMES, which cannot express the invariant it "
"was asked to enforce: a file called 'holiday-photo-not-an-invoice.png' "
"satisfied a requirement named 'Invoice', and a genuine invoice scanned to "
"'scan001.pdf' did not."
msgstr ""

#. module: approval
#: model:ir.model.fields,help:approval.field_approval_approver__decided_by_user_id
msgid ""
"Who actually made the decision recorded in decision_date — the delegate when"
" the row was decided inside an active delegation window, otherwise user_id "
"itself. The pair (user_id, decided_by_user_id) separates WHOSE approval slot"
" this is from WHO exercised it; every other identity question in the module "
"resolves the effective approver, and without this column the analytics were "
"the one place that could not: approver.performance credited the delegated "
"decision (and its response time) to the absent principal while the delegate "
"who did the work scored nothing. Left empty for rows flipped by non-"
"decisions, exactly like decision_date, and cleared beside it on withdraw and"
" reset-to-draft."
msgstr ""

#. module: approval
#: model:ir.model.fields,help:approval.field_approval_category__privacy_visibility
msgid ""
"Who may READ the requests of this category (additive on top of\n"
"        the always-allowed requester/approvers/delegate and managers):\n"
"\n"
"        • Only people involved: no extra read audience (requester, approvers\n"
"          and delegates always retain access regardless of this setting).\n"
"        • Restricted to selected users: the users in 'Allowed Users' may\n"
"          read every request in the category.\n"
"        • Restricted to selected groups: members of the groups in\n"
"          'Allowed Groups' may read every request in the category.\n"
"        • All internal users: every internal user may read every request.\n"
"\n"
"        The 'restricted_*' modes read the audience from the SAME 'Allowed\n"
"        Users'/'Allowed Groups' lists that gate request creation, and those\n"
"        lists mean \"everyone\" only while they are EMPTY. So choosing a\n"
"        restricted mode is not a read-only decision: to name an audience you\n"
"        must fill a list in, and filling it in restricts creation to exactly\n"
"        those people. There is deliberately no way to say \"anyone may\n"
"        request, only this group may read\" — that would need an audience\n"
"        list separate from the create-gate. Widening read access to a\n"
"        supervisor group therefore also hands that group exclusive rights to\n"
"        file in the category; if that is not what you want, keep the category\n"
"        'Only people involved' and give the supervisors the Administrator\n"
"        group instead, which reads everything without touching creation."
msgstr ""

